# R38 `&self` mutation-inference — PRECISION: a read-only `&self` chain on
# a NAMED receiver must STAY read-only (no over-clone, hence no clone bomb).
#
# `describe` has no direct self-write; it only calls the getter `get_name`
# on `self`. The fixpoint classifies BOTH `Rec__get_name` and (transitively)
# `Rec__describe` READ-ONLY, so the NAMED-receiver call `r.describe()` is
# NOT materialized. The output is correct either way (a read cannot be
# written through), but the classification keeps the hot self-compile loops
# from deep-cloning every `&self` getter receiver — the ~12GB clone bomb the
# blanket `&self`-implies-mutating over-approx would produce (peak RSS is the
# real precision guard). Correct output: A then A.
struct Rec:
    String name

equip Rec:
    String get_name(&self):
        return self.name

    String describe(&self):
        return self.get_name()

void main():
    Rec r = Rec("A")
    print(r.describe())   # A  (read-only chain)
    print(r.name)         # A
